A rich preview of a link, shown while it's hovered or focused.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/preview-card)

<%= embed UI::PreviewCardPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
p do
  plain "Built by "
  PreviewCard do
    PreviewCardTrigger(href: user_path(@user), class: "text-primary font-medium") { "@#{@user.handle}" }
    PreviewCardContent(class: "w-72") { render UserCardComponent.new(@user) }
  end
end
```

The trigger stays a real `<a>` - a click navigates. The card opens after 600 ms on hover or keyboard focus and closes
300 ms after the pointer leaves the link and the card (`delay:` / `close_delay:` on the root). It sits inside a
paragraph without breaking it: the root is a `<span>` and the card is kept in a `<template>` until the controller
connects. It's invisible on touch and to screen readers, so keep it supplementary.

